 filename←root FindFileInSourceFolder token;source;list;bool;ind;caption
⍝ Searches the source folder of the project in `root` for a file named `token` and returns its
⍝ name relative to `root`, or an empty vector in case there is no match at all.\\
⍝ `token` must be a filename without any path information, like `Add.aplf`.\\
⍝ When there is more than one match the user is asked which one she means; quitting that
⍝ selection returns an empty vector as well.
 filename←''
 root←NormalizeFolder root
 :If 0<≢source←GetSourceFolder root
 :AndIf 0<≢list←⊃('recursive' 2)F.Dir root,'/',source,'*'
     list←F.EnforceSlash¨list
     bool←(⊂⎕C token)≡¨⎕C¨{∊1↓⎕NPARTS ⍵}¨list
     list←bool/list
     :Select ≢list
     :Case 0
     :Case 1
         filename←⊃list
     :Else
         caption←'SelectFileForAPLGit2@There is more than one file called "',token,'" - which one do you mean?'
         ind←caption ##.CommTools.Select list
         :If 0<≢ind
             filename←ind⊃list
         :EndIf
     :EndSelect
 :EndIf
 :If 0<≢filename
     filename←(1+≢root)↓filename
 :EndIf
⍝Done
